From 97c82a45e769f69ed129ee1237cf2931ba234dd3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kernel86-64 <87580651+kernel86-64@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 17:20:31 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 58/59] arm64: configs: joan: enable CONFIG_ASHMEM and memfd
 ashmem shim

Enable CONFIG_ASHMEM=y (which selects CONFIG_ASHMEM_C=y and defaults CONFIG_MEMFD_ASHMEM_SHIM=y) in joan_defconfig.

Inside isolated WebView renderer sandboxes (e.g. LineageOS Jelly), libcutils cannot readlink(/proc/self/fd/...) due to EPERM and falls back to issuing ASHMEM_* ioctls (such as ASHMEM_SET_PROT_MASK / 0x7705) directly on memfd file descriptors. Without CONFIG_ASHMEM and CONFIG_MEMFD_ASHMEM_SHIM, shmem_ashmem_ioctl is compiled out, causing ENOTTY and stalling CrRendererMain at 100% CPU with a grey screen.
---
 arch/arm64/configs/joan_defconfig | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/joan_defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/joan_defconfig
index d33b8fdbc..35771bb8f 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/joan_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/joan_defconfig
@@ -1113,6 +1113,7 @@ CONFIG_XEN_GRANT_DEV_ALLOC=y
 CONFIG_GREYBUS=m
 CONFIG_GREYBUS_BEAGLEPLAY=m
 CONFIG_STAGING=y
+CONFIG_ASHMEM=y
 CONFIG_STAGING_MEDIA=y
 CONFIG_VIDEO_MAX96712=m
 CONFIG_CHROME_PLATFORMS=y
